+        "\n" +
+        "Each step **restarts the defender's animation** (ANO). The empty slots of the character (no rows) can be filled with the app (copy from the game data, copy from another slot, import from another character, or blank).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 5.5 HDAT 4 — fields of a move (`$GOLPE_i`)\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "{{HDAT4_TABLE}}\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**`ATK_FLAGS` bits** (sum the values you want):\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "| Bit | Name | Effect |\n" +
+        "|---|---|---|\n" +
+        "| 1 | GROUND_ONLY | the projectile explodes only on the floor (does not explode on the enemy) |\n" +
+        "| 2 | NO_TRADE | the move's hitbox destroys the opponent's hitboxes (the opponent enters the reaction stored in the character's HDAT 3 byte 13) |\n" +
+        "| 4 | TRIPLE | throws 3 projectiles (ANO, ANO+1, ANO+2) |\n" +
+        "| 8 | GRAB | grab at the end of `ANIM_INICIAL` or during a frame with the window bit 512; continues to `ANIM_INICIAL + 1`; works even if it did not hit. The app shows it in the **transition lane** (`AGARRAR → ANO`) and as the \"Tentar agarrão\" object; the grab distance is HDAT 3 byte 5 (`$DISTANCIA_AGARRE` in `$STATUS_BASE_E_FISICA` of `000.bin.txt`, px), editable in both menus |\n" +
+        "| 16 | GHOST | characters pass through each other |\n" +
+        "| 32 | PROJ_OPP | the projectile spawns at the opponent (turns off 64) |\n" +
+        "| 64 | PROJ_FLOOR | the projectile spawns under the opponent, stuck to the floor (turns off 32) |\n" +
+        "| 128 | GRAB_HIT | grab only while the opponent is in this move's hurt reaction (moves 0..12 only; if the move has a sequence the sequence takes over and the grab does not happen) |\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "Move indexes: moves **0, 3 and 6** are special slots; when transplanting a move to another character, 0/3/6 can only replace 0/3/6 and the others only the non-special ones. Grabs only work in moves 0..12. Move text fields are 16-bit: **ANO numbers above 255 are normal** (up to 32767).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 5.6 Sounds\n" +
+        "Sound id `SE` (an **unsigned byte, 0–255**; values above 127 only work in a `TCBManajer` patched for that): 0 = none; 1..79 = common game sounds `se_00`..`se_78` (file = id − 1; the app's sound list plays them); **80..99 = the character's own `*.wav` files in sorted file-name order** (first wav = 80, at most 20); 100..255 = new common sounds `se_99`..`se_254` (file names have 3 digits from `se_100.ogg`). Files `se_79`..`se_99` are silent filler (the game loads the `se_` files in sequence, never delete one); the first new global sound after `se_78` is `se_100` (id 101). The app adds global sounds as **Opus inside .ogg** (Android 10+). Voice in reactions uses the same ids (1..127). Adding/removing wavs shifts ids — warn the user before suggesting that.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 5.7 Sprites and the CNV\n" +
+        "Frame `$IMG: n` → `$SPR_n` in `000.cnv.txt` → rectangle in sheet `NNN.png` (`$src`). A `.cnv` outside the PAC is plain text (`CNV_TXT_ { $SPR_n:{$src:…, $x:…, …} }`) with the **original** coordinates (no ×2); `.cnv.txt` holds the **final** coordinates (already ×2 for characters). Either can be used as the source when importing sprites from another pac. `$src` is the **index** of the sheet in the folder's list of `NNN.png` files sorted by name — not the number in the file name: with `017.png`, `018.cnv`, `019.png`, `$src:18` is `019.png`. The sprite list screen (`SPRITES`) adds/replaces/removes sprites, edits cuts and imports PNG/JPG/GIF; new sprites go to the first free space of a sheet. Sheets are never rewritten destructively.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 5.8 Linked animations (links) and effects\n" +
+        "A link spawns another ANO together with its parent (effects, body parts, auras) and follows it. Only 1 level, max 13 per ANO. Effects can also be triggered by hit flags 10–17 / 41–125 (see 5.2).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "## 6. How a move works in the game (what you need to design one)\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 6.1 Time\n" +
+        "60 ticks per second. A frame lasts `$TIME` ticks; an ANO ends after its last frame (unless the last frames are looped/redirected by a sequence). A frame **without `$TIME` freezes forever** and also does not add acceleration.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 6.2 Movement (speed and acceleration)\n" +
+        "- `SPEED` = constant pixels per tick while the frame lasts (`speed 50` for 5 ticks = 250 px; in text, decimals like `2.5` are px/tick).\n" +
+        "- `ACCEL` adds its value to the speed **every tick after the object moved**: accel 50 for 5 ticks from rest moves 0, 50, 100, 150, 200 = 500 px and ends at speed 250.\n" +
+        "- On loading each frame the game **zeroes speed and accel**, unless the frame has `$WACTFLAG` bit **64** (\"keep speed\"): then the frame starts with the speed the previous frame ended with (its speed + accumulated acceleration). A received speed counts as speed (a frame's own `$XSPEED` replaces it); accel is never inherited, so write it again in every frame that needs it.\n" +
+        "- A jump is written as several frames: first frame with a negative `$YSPEED` (up) and a positive `$YACCEL` (gravity), the following frames with `$WACTFLAG: 64` so the speed carries over.\n" +
+        "- Linked animations and frames synchronised with the parent (0x2000/0x8000) do not move by themselves.\n" +
+        "- The editor's `Movimento` page and the `Σ` total show the pixels travelled.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 6.3 Hits, damage and reactions\n" +
+        "A **hitbox** (flag 2) in a frame whose `$OPT` has `d0` = damage and `d1` = reaction code (`group*50+index`) hits when it overlaps the opponent's **hurtbox** (flag 1); the same hit does not re-hit within the same frame. The hit applies the damage, plays hit effect/sound/hitstop by the reaction **group** (5.4) and puts the opponent in the **reaction** (a list of steps with the opponent's own ANOs and velocities). A hit also triggers the move's **sequence** if defined. A hitbox is always **one object per Frame** in the timeline (the hit repeats on every Frame, even with identical boxes); hurtbox, projectile, effect and action boxes with equal values across consecutive Frames still join into one object.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 6.4 Sequences (combos inside a move)\n" +
+        "HDAT 4 fields: `ANIM_SEQ_CHAO` / `ANIM_SEQ_AR` = ANO to go to when a hit connects while the attacker is on the ground / in the air; `ANIM_END_CHAO` / `ANIM_END_AR` = ANO to go to when a **new** hit connects while in the SEQ ANO (the END ANO itself has no further transition); `ANIM_AO_ACERTAR` (SEQ_PROJETIL) = ANO the attacker goes to when a **projectile's first hit** connects. A hit with flag 38 prevents the SEQ from firing. A SEQ may not point to its own ANO. If you define only ground or only air the app asks whether to use the same ANO for the other.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 6.5 Landing\n" +
+        "`POUSO_AO_ERRAR` / `POUSO_AO_ACERTAR` = ANO the attacker switches to when it touches the floor after a missed / connected aerial move. The `POUSO` button of the app toggles this in the preview.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 6.6 Projectiles\n" +
+        "A frame with flag 0 spawns the projectile ANO chosen from the HDAT 4 by the height difference between attacker and opponent: `PROJETIL_ANIM_NORMAL` (near the same height), `..._ABAIXO` (the **attacker** is ≥ 51 px lower than the opponent), `..._ACIMA` (the attacker is ≥ 37 px higher). `PROJETIL_ANIM_AO_ACERTAR` = the projectile's hit-reaction ANO, `PROJETIL_COLISAO_CHAO` = floor-collision ANO, `PROJETIL_ANIM_ACERTAR_GLOBAL` = global-hit ANO. A projectile ANO may itself contain flag 0 frames that spawn **sub-projectiles** (`SUBPROJETIL_*`). The main projectile spawns at attacker x + hit x (if it would land behind the attacker the game throws it 480 px ahead, so the minimum x is 0). `HOMING` + `HOMING_VELOCIDADE` make it chase the opponent; `MAX_REPETICOES` > 0 repeats the projectile (uses the 512 window, so a repeating move cannot also use \"try grab\"). **Max 8 live projectiles**; spawning with 8 alive creates nothing silently.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 6.7 Effects and auras\n" +
+        "Hit flags 10–17, 41–70 and 71–125 spawn effects/auras while the flag is present in the frame (5.2). For your own effect: make an ANO numbered `201 + (flag − 71)` in the character and put a hit with that flag (offset x,y) in the frames where it should be visible.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 6.7b Dust / smoke ($OPT flag bits 4096-32768)\n" +
+        "The `$OPT` flag bits 12-15 (value / 4096) are the dust **type 1-15**: one smoke is created per frame loaded, standing still in the world at the object's position (ANO +80 when the object is facing left; at most 6 alive at once, the 7th removes the oldest). Types 1-5 = `bobj` pack ANOs 10-14; 6-7 = `effect` ANOs 78-79; 8-15 = `effect` ANOs 70-77. A smoke ANO can spawn child smokes: each of its hits (flag N) creates `bobj` ANO N+70 at the hit's x/y. The app draws them and previews each type in the action menu. In the effects lane clips are labelled `effect N` / `charf N` / `char N` (N = ANO of that pack).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 6.8 Interpolation and transforms\n" +
+        "`$RAZ` (rotation, alpha, zoom) can be interpolated toward the next frame by `$OPT` d2 ≠ 0. The flag belongs to the frame that has it: that frame goes to the NEXT one (the frame before does not interpolate to it); on a frame without time it does nothing; on the LAST frame the \"next\" wraps to frame 1 (even without LOOP). The next frame should have the same number of boxes.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 6.9 Camera, shake, cutscenes\n" +
+        "Flags 3–5 (shake), 30/31 (zoom) and 20 (cutscene) act on the camera. Cutscenes are driven by data tables of the character (HDAT 13) — don't invent them; reuse an existing event.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "## 7. Limits (computed from the app's own validator; **the game crashes/closes when a \"fatal\" one is exceeded**)\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "{{LIMITS}}\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "Other facts: ANOs referenced by links are 12-bit (max 4095); HDAT 4 values are 16-bit (max 32767); reaction table columns are 1 byte (ANO −128..127, voice 1..127 effective, durations 0..255, speeds −128..127); sprite index must exist in the CNV or the frame draws nothing; reaction slots of a character: 20 (HDAT 14..33), and the `$HDAT_14+n` block must already exist in `000.bin.txt` to be written by the app (it creates the missing `$REACAO_DANO_n` inside it).\n" +
