+        "**Per-tick order [CODE].** `Run` iterates the task list in ascending priority (ties in creation order): pads (12657/12660) → input md 946 (13056+p) → macro/CPU md 947/951 (13184+) → projectiles md 970/971 (13312+p) → **fighters (13569+p)** → hit effects md 965 (13598) → shadows/auras (13696+) → **hit detect md 935 (13728)** → **cutscene md 996 (13729)** → camera md 19 (13745) → HUD (13808+). So within a tick: input → projectiles → fighters (new patterns load, hit boxes become armed) → hit detect (reads those boxes) → camera. A reaction chosen by `DamageChange` in md 935 starts running on the defender's **next** tick. A task created during the pass with a lower priority than the running one first runs on the next tick (a projectile spawned by a fighter advances one tick later). With `bTaskSkip` (pause) only priorities `0x10xx` run; with `iTaskSleep != 0` or `bActionStop` all `0x3xxx` tasks (12288–16383: fighters, projectiles, hit detect, camera) are skipped (hit-stop of the whole scene, cutscene freezes).\n" +
