+        "",
+        "**Other tables used by attacks [CODE].** HDAT 3 (body data, row 0): byte 0/1 forward/back speed, byte 3 body width (half used for walls), byte 4 `PlayerYLimit`, byte 5 grab distance, byte 6 `AirType`/\"can fly\", byte 7 dash speed, byte 10 charge gain, byte 12/14 attack/defense base, **byte 13 clash reaction** (the reaction a hitbox with `ATK_FLAGS` bit 2 forces on the opponent), byte 16 sealed-art ANO. HDAT 13: cutscene rows (stride `2*XSize[13]` bytes). HDAT 14–33 (character) / 10–39 (gamedata): reactions, 14 columns (15.5). HDAT 6: CPU sequences. HDAT 5: score and combo-scaling table. HDAT 37/35: rage multiplier and event damage.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**ANO / DAC structure [CODE].** `ObjReq.acttype` is the `ChrGameData` index (fighter p+3, effects 5, common 0); `acttype & 0xFF000` marks pseudo-sprites skipped by `_ActReqMain` (jogo:31773). `_SetAct` (jogo:32325): `getData(3)` is the raw `dac` chunk: `[2]` = ANO count (short), `[4]` = ANO table offset, `[6]` = entry data base; the pointer is `short @ table + ano*2` (−1 = absent); the entry is at `(ptr << 2) + base`: byte 0 = flags (4 = priority byte present, 2 = link block), byte 1 = `mpt` (pattern count) (jogo:32354-32366). Links are 6 bytes each (x, y, flags|ANO & 4095); up to 13 (`lnk[13]`). **Calling `_SetAct` with the same `ano` and `acttype` is a no-op** (jogo:32338) — that is why the game sets `objExec.ano = 0` first to restart. A missing ANO leaves `apt = 0` and the next `_ActReq` sets `wActFlag |= 2` (the move ends next tick). Pattern fields: see 15.8.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Alignment, sentinels, limits an editor must respect [CODE].** All multi-byte values are little-endian; `piGameData` is a `short[]` of **unsigned bytes** (the code casts `(byte)` for signed reads: reaction ANO, speeds, voice); ANO numbers in links are 12-bit (≤ 4095); `hit[50]` = 10 boxes max per frame; `lnk[13]`; pattern count 1 byte (255); `time` 1 byte; `OptData` 4 bytes; OPT1 ≥ 250 crashes (`HitEffectActNo[5]`); reaction `COMP ≥ 30` in md 876 reads out-of-range tables; `-1` ANO = absent; `-1`/`-2` in reaction speeds are sentinels (15.5). **Local vs. global indices**: ANO numbers in a character's HDAT 4 / links / DAC are **local to that character's DAC**; hit flags 10–17 use the **effect pack** (ANO 50 + flag − 10), flags 41–70 use the **charf pack** (ANO flag − 41 + 3), flags 71–125 use the **character's own DAC** (ANO 201 + flag − 71); reaction types 0–29 are global (gamedata), 30–49 are the attacker's own table. **Differences between characters/versions**: none found in the code (one code path for all `char##`); data differ only in the pacs **[INFERRED]**.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 15.3 Hitboxes, hurtboxes and collision (questions 16–24)\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Box types [CODE].** A frame's hit list is up to **10** entries of five shorts `(type, x, y, w, h)` in `hit[50]` (`type & 127`; if bit 128 of the type is set the fields are 16-bit, else bytes; jogo:31944-31981). Type **1** = hurtbox, type **2** = hitbox (attack box), type **0** = projectile spawn marker (x/y = spawn offset). Every other type is an *action marker* processed by `CheckOptFlag` (flags 3–5, 20, 26–28, 30–34, 37–40, 10–17, 41–125; list in 15.10); its `x,y,w,h` are parameters, not geometry. So there are only two collision box kinds: attack (2) and hurt (1) — plus attack-vs-attack for clashes.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Geometry [CODE]** (`CheckObjHit`, jogo:2045-2110): horizontal mirror flag `m = (wActFlag & 48) ^ (wObjFlag & 48)`. For the box of object `o`: if `(m & 16) != 0` the box spans `x ∈ [ox - hx - hw, ox - hx]`, else `[ox + hx, ox + hx + hw]` (`ox = o.x >> 16`, integer pixels; `hx, hw` = the box's x and width). Vertically, if `(m & 32) != 0` it spans `[oy - hy - hh, oy - hy]` else `[oy + hy, oy + hy + hh]`. **y grows downward.** Coordinates are relative to the object's position (the character's `PlayerXPos/YPos`, i.e. the foot point), **not** to the sprite origin (`$MID`) or to the image. Facing left (`wObjFlag & 16`) mirrors X; a flipped animation (`wActFlag` bit 16) mirrors again (XOR).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Intersection test [CODE].** Strict inequalities on all four edges: `a.left < b.right && b.left < a.right && a.top < b.bottom && b.top < a.bottom`; **touching edges do not hit**. No tolerance, no priority, no rounding beyond integer pixels. The function returns on the **first** overlapping pair (loops attacker boxes then defender boxes, in list order) and stores the hit point `iHitXPos/iHitYPos` = midpoint of the two box centres (used for the hit effect). Only the **root object's** boxes are tested — linked sub-objects (`lnk[]`) are not.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**When boxes are tested [CODE].** Only boxes of the **currently loaded pattern** exist (`hit[]` is rebuilt at every pattern load; the flag-bit-16 block of that frame). A pattern without a hit block has `iHitNum = 0` and `iHitCount = 0`. Hit detection runs every tick in md 935 once `bGameStart`; both players must have life > 0 and neither may be in md 923/926/927/928/911 (jogo:23542-23547).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**One hit per pattern; no repeated hits [CODE].** Arming: when a pattern with a hit block is loaded the root's `TCB.iHitCount = 1` and `TCB.iHitFlag` = bitmask of box types; on any resolved hit `iHitCount` is zeroed for both players (jogo:23480; projectiles jogo:23415-23416; clash jogo:23313). Consequently a hitbox that stays active for many frames of **one** pattern hits **once**; a **multi-hit** move is a sequence of **patterns each carrying a hit block** (each re-arms and applies full damage again with combo scaling). A pattern that misses keeps testing every tick for its `time`. There is **no per-target or per-box \"already hit\" register**; the whole mechanism is `iHitCount`. Hit-stop is applied to both fighters (`iHitStop = PlayerHitStop[atk]`).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Simultaneous cases [CODE].** *Two boxes in one frame*: the first overlapping pair wins. *Both players hit each other in the same tick* (trade): both `DamageChange` calls run with **OPT1 forced to 0** (jogo:23457-23459); the body-hit loop runs victim 0 then victim 1 so index 1 wins a double KO. *Clash* (attack box vs attack box, `CheckObjHit(…, true)`): skipped if either ANO is 27/28; needs opposite facing, `iTimer > 0`, and both ANOs < 40 or both ≥ 40 (jogo:23289-23306); both fighters get hit-stop, both `iHitCount` are cleared, spark effect 3 and SE 9 play (unless a participant is in md 911–915), **no damage**; if a participant has `SpecialKind & 2` (\"NO_TRADE\") the opponent is forced into the reaction from the counter-user's `charHDAT3[0][13]` (types ≥ 30 → md 877 else md 876; jogo:23486-23516). *Projectile vs fighter*: a projectile that overlaps a defender's attack box (defender ANO ≥ 40) is absorbed with no damage if the defender's `OptData[0] % 50 != 0` (jogo:23390-23402); projectile attack boxes against each other cancel (SE 9, jogo:23430-23443).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Invulnerability, dodge, teleport, throws, guard [CODE].** Hits are skipped when the defender's `wObjFlag & 8` (set on alternating frames during md 876 hit-stop, md 898/899 invulnerable pose and the ThrowDamage path, which is dead code), when either life ≤ 0, in md 923/926/927/928/911, and obviously when the defender's current frame has no type-1 box (an invulnerable animation is simply one without hurtboxes). Evades (SpecialType 18/19) vanish via md 865. Hit flags 39/40 teleport instantly (`CheckOptFlag`). Guard: see 15.4. Throws are ordinary hits plus the \"grabbed overlay\" objects (md 939–941) that hit through the projectile path (jogo:23424).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Walls and screen [CODE].** Variables: `iBackXPos` (camera left in world px·65536), `iBaseXPos` (base position: 0 = left world edge, 62849024 = right), `iBackXOffset` (camera offset used by cutscenes), `DamageWall` (a reaction hit the wall), `bForceWall` (forces wall detection anywhere; reset every tick in md 935 and set by cutscene kind 6). Details of the wall test and the WALL/COMP behaviour are in 15.5 and 15.6.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 15.4 Damage and life loss (questions 25–33)\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "Source of truth: the game class `TCBManajer` (file `TCBManajer.java`, \"jogo:NNNN\" = line). Tags: **[CODE]** read in the game code, **[INFERRED]** deduced, **[UNKNOWN]** not determinable from the code. The game is strictly **1 vs 1**: \"several targets\" does not exist.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Call chain [CODE].** The hit-resolution task is md 935 (`case 935:` jogo:23194), run every tick. Damage and reaction are read from the attacker's `ObjReq` at hit time: `OptData[0]` = damage, `OptData[1]` = OPT1 (loaded per animation pattern in `_ActReqMain`, jogo:31993-32014; a pattern with no `$OPT` block gets `wOptFlag = 0` and `OptData[0..3] = 0`, so a hitbox frame without `$OPT` deals **0 damage with OPT1 = 0** — group 0, reaction 0 — and still counts as a hit). `DamageChange(gw, atk, tgt, bApply, bBody, atkAno, dmgByte, opt1, optFlag)` (jogo:3466) is called for projectiles and grab follow-up objects at jogo:23424 and for body hits at jogo:23464. If both players hit each other in the same tick, OPT1 is **forced to 0 for both** (jogo:23457-23459: a trade always uses reaction 0 / effect-sound group 0). The body-hit loop runs victim 0 first then victim 1; if player 1's hit KOs player 0, player 0's own hit is skipped by the early-out \"attacker life ≤ 0\" at jogo:3478-3480, so **index 1 wins a double KO**.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**`$OPT` bytes [CODE].** `d0` = base damage 0..255 (jogo:3496; also the heal amount of hit flag 34 at jogo:2313 and the self-damage amount of flag 32 at jogo:23261). `d1` = OPT1 = `group*50+index` (jogo:3518-3519). `d2` ≠ 0 turns on the per-pattern tween of rotation/alpha/zoom/offset (`_Hokan`, jogo:32108; visual only). `d3` is written and **never read**. OPT1 values **250..255 index `HitEffectActNo[5]` out of range → the game crashes** (jogo:3529); the editor limit is 249.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Formula [CODE], all integer math, left-to-right truncation:**\n" +
+        "1. If the attacker has hit flag 28 active (`PlayerState & 262144`): `D1 = D0` (no multipliers, no minimum).\n" +
+        "2. Else if `D0 != 0`: `def = DeffenceMul[tgt] + AddDeffencePer[tgt]` (the second term is never written, always 0); `def = max(def, 0)`; `D1 = AttackMul[atk] * D0 / 100 * (100 - def) / 100` (jogo:3496); if the attacker is in rage (`AngryOn[atk]`) `D1 = charHDAT37[0][0] * D1 / 100` (jogo:3498-3500); `if (D1 < 2) D1 = 2` (jogo:3503-3505). If `D0 == 0`, `D1 = 0`.\n" +
+        "3. If the attacker's ANO is **92**, `D1 = 0` (the hit and reaction still happen; jogo:3514).\n" +
+        "4. **Combo scaling** (jogo:3529-3560): `c = ComboCount[atk]` (before this hit); `idx = c` if c < 2 else `min(c,15) - 2` (sequence for c = 0,1,2,3,4… is idx 0,1,0,1,2,…,13); if `D1 != 0`: `D2 = (short)LE16(gamedata HDAT 5, row 2, idx) * D1 / 100`, and `D2 = 1` if the result is 0. Applies to flag-28 hits too. The table values live in the data pac **[UNKNOWN]**.\n" +
+        "5. Cap and apply on hit only (jogo:3806-3815): `D3 = min(D2, Life[tgt])`; `TotalDamage[tgt] += D3`; `LIFE_DEC(tgt, D3)` (jogo:3878; `LIFE_DEC` at jogo:29164 acts only when `iTimer != 0` and the other player is alive). `Life` is clamped ≥ 0 (≥ 1 in `iPlayMode == 2` and in mission-life checks).\n" +
+        "6. Side effects of `D3`: defender gauge `SYNCHRO_ADD(tgt, charHDAT1[0][3]*D3/charHDAT1[0][2])` and `ANGRY_ADD(tgt, 10)`; attacker gauge `charHDAT1[0][1]*D3/charHDAT1[0][0]`; score (animations 27..66, not flag 37).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Attack/defense stats [CODE].** `AttackMul[p] = GetAttack + GetCardAttack` (jogo:5513-5515); `GetAttack` (jogo:27721) = `charHDAT3[0][12]` + sum of `charHDAT7[i][1]` for i up to `min(Level+AddLevel, 98)`; `GetDeffence` (jogo:28191) = `[0][14]` + sum of `[i][3]`. Values are percentages [INFERRED from `/100`]. **No term depends on distance, the defender's state/position or the move's index** — only `AttackMul`, `DeffenceMul`, rage, combo count, animation 92 and flag 28.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Hit flags that change damage [CODE].** 26 = skip the guard check (unblockable). 27 = blocks the cancel logic while `CancelTime > 0`. 28 = raw damage (above). 32 = self-damage frame: when `iHitCount != 0`, both alive and `PlayerState & 1048576` (jogo:23260-23263) → `SelfDamage(p, OptData[0], OptData[1])` (jogo:30833), which sets `Life = 1` if `Life <= d` (it **cannot kill**) and ignores attack/defense. 33 = sets a state bit nobody reads (no effect). 34 = heal: `LIFE_ADD(p, OptData[0])` (capped at max life; needs `iTimer != 0` and the opponent alive). 37 = no combo count and no score (damage still uses combo scaling). 38 = chain uses `DamageHitActNo` instead of the HDAT 4 lookup. These bits live in `PlayerState[player]` and are **cleared every tick and re-applied from the current pattern** (`PlayerTail`, jogo:29884), so they only matter in frames that carry the hit flag.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Guard [CODE].** Defender states allowed to guard: not in md 876/877, ANO not in {6,7,8,9,82,83}, ANO ≤ 19 or in {25,80,81}, `iTimer != 0`, attacker has no flag 26 (jogo:3562-3585). Humans guard by holding a direction away from the attacker; CPUs use probabilities; **height (high/low) is ignored**. On guard: no reaction table, `DamageMove = GuardHitBack` (13, groups < 3), `GuardCancelTime = PlayerHitStop + 5`, chip damage only if the attacker's ANO ≥ 40: `max(D2/5, 1)` scaled by `GuardHardness` (never written → 0) then `max(.., 2)` when `D2 != 0`; no combo increment; hit effect Ano 2 with SE 8.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Never-assigned values [CODE].** `AddDeffencePer`, `GuardHardness`, `SynchroAttackPer` are read but never written (always 0); `DamageHitBack` is only ever assigned 0 (the hit push-back is always 0); `ThrowDamage` (jogo:187) is **never set to true** anywhere — every `ThrowDamage == true` branch is dead code in this build.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Per-event rules [CODE].** Damage is applied **once per resolved hit event**, and a hit event happens at most **once per animation pattern** (next section). Projectile damage uses the **owner's** `AttackMul` and `PlayerState`; projectile hit flags land on the owner's `PlayerState`. A projectile that overlaps a defender's attack box (defender ANO ≥ 40) is absorbed with no damage if the defender's `OptData[0] % 50 != 0` (jogo:23390-23402); projectile vs projectile attack boxes cancel with SE 9 (jogo:23430-23443).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**KO and hitstop [CODE].** If `Life[tgt] <= 0` after damage the OPT1 reaction is **overridden**: `DamageType = 2, DamageIndex = 0, DamageTime = 0, DamageOldType = 2`, md 876 (jogo:3993-4000); in md 876 a KO in type 2 becomes type 29 (jogo:20989-20992); after the reaction the game plays ANO 24 and enters md 888 → 889 and stays down. Hitstop: `iHitStop = PlayerHitStop[atk]` for **both** players (6 for basic attacks, 10 for specials); group 3 uses half for body hits, group 4 none; projectiles give the target full hitstop and the projectile half; it decrements at the start of md 935 and pauses animation and reaction movement; in md 876 hitstop the defender jitters ±1 px. Invulnerable when: defender `wObjFlag & 8` (alternating frames in md 876 hitstop), either player's life ≤ 0, either player in md 923/926/927/928/911 (the whole hit step is skipped), `iTimer == 0` (no life loss). Hits **during a reaction are allowed** (no untechable window): `DamageChange` resets `DamageTime/Index` and re-enters the reaction.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**What the app's simulator omits [CODE-compared].** `BattleSim.applyDamage` matches flag 28, min-2, ANO 92, combo scaling, life cap and combo count; it omits the rage multiplier, guard/chip, score and gauge gain.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 15.5 Reactions, COMP and recovery (questions 34–45)\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Resolving OPT1 [CODE].** `group = OPT1 / 50`, `index = OPT1 % 50` (jogo:3518-3519). `index >= 30` → md 877 with `DamageType = index - 30` and the **attacker's** character table HDAT 14+type; `index < 30` → md 876 with `DamageType = index` and the gamedata table HDAT 10+type (jogo:3824-3828, 20995, 21264). Example: **OPT1 116 = group 2 (strong), index 16 = game-wide reaction 16**; OPT1 52 = group 1, index 2.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Groups [CODE].** `HitEffectActNo = {0,0,1,0,-1}`, `HitSound = {3,4,6,3,7}`, `GuardEffectActNo = {2,2,2,2,-1}` (jogo:601-603). Group 4: no effect, no sound, no combo increment. Push-back (`DamageMove`) only for groups < 3 and it is always 0. Hitstop: group 3 half (body hits), group 4 none. Combo count (cap 99) increments only when the effect ANO is 0 or 1 and the hit is not flag 37. Sound is SE 8 for any effect other than ANO 0/1, else `HitSound[group]`. A hit with OPT1 forced by a trade or clash is always group 0.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Where the tables are [CODE].** Gamedata HDAT 10..39 come from the data pac `gamedata` (`InitGameData`, jogo:29133-29134); character tables are HDAT 14..33 inside `ChrGameData[player+3]`. **No reaction rows are literals in the code**; all rows are in the data pacs. Table header = u16 count then 8-byte entries {pos u32, xsize u16, ysize u16}; each reaction is its own table with xsize 14 and ysize = number of steps. `piGameData` is a `short[]` of unsigned bytes; the code casts `(byte)` where it needs signed.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**The 14 columns [CODE].** 0 `DUR_C` (ticks while `PlayerYPos == 15728640`, i.e. on the ground); 1 `DUR_A` (ticks while airborne or below the floor, jogo:21201-21207); 2 `ANO` (signed; negative flips the defender: `wObjFlag ^= 16` and uses `-ano`, jogo:21002-21008); 3–6 ground `xspeed, yspeed, xaccel, yaccel` (signed); 7–10 the same for air (used when `PlayerYPos < 15728640`); 11 `COMP`; 12 `WALL`; 13 `VOZ` (signed; `> 0` plays `Voice(1, player, v)` when the row is entered, jogo:20996-20999).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Special values [CODE].** *Speeds/accels:* `-1` keeps the current `DamageX/YSpeed`/`Accel` (jogo:21033-21060); `-2` on a speed = `rawUnsigned(OldType row OldIndex, same column) / 2` (**raw, not scaled by 128/10, and read as an unsigned byte** — a quirk: a previous speed of −40 is read as 216); `-2` on an accel = half of the current accel. Normal values are `v*128/10` (truncating): one unit = 1/128 px per tick scaled by 10, i.e. tenths of a pixel per tick (`v = 10` → 1 px/tick). *Duration 255:* the row holds until `DamageTime >= 255`, then switches to `DamageType 2, Index 0` (in md 877 type 2 reads the attacker's character table HDAT 16; jogo:21208-21213, 21492-21496). *Duration 0:* lasts 1 tick (`max(dur,1)`).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "",
+        "**Row stepping [CODE].** Entering a row loads speeds (`DamageTime` 0 → 1); each non-hitstop tick checks `DamageTime >= dur`, otherwise `DamageTime++`; at the end of a row `DamageIndex++`, `DamageTime = 0` (jogo:21215-21217). Hitstop ticks do not advance the row (the entry load still runs). Past the last row: still moving vertically (`DamageYSpeed != 0`) → alive: type 13 (md 877 explicitly switches to md 876); dead: type 2 / lying; `DamageYSpeed == 0` → alive: `DamageEnd` and md 864 (control returns); dead: ANO 24, md 888.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**COMP [CODE]** — evaluated every tick after movement when `iHitStop == 0` (jogo:21095-21200, 21369-21482):\n" +
+        "- **0**: if `PlayerYPos > 15728640` clamp to the ground and clear `PlayerAir`; nothing else.\n" +
+        "- **1..49 with `WALL` not 2/3 and `!bForceWall`**: COMP **11** → when `Y > ground` or (`YSpeed <= 0` and `YAccel <= 0`): `Y = ground`, ANO 24, md 888 (lying). Otherwise, on reaching the ground (`Y >= ground`): snap, play SE 11; if COMP is 12 and `DefensiveFlag == 1` (the player pressed a mask-16640 button while airborne) and alive → `DamageEnd`, ANO 22, md 886 (air tech); else switch `DamageType = comp`, `Index 0`, `Time 0`. In md 877 `comp >= 30` switches to the attacker's character table `comp - 30`; below 30 it goes to md 876 gamedata type `comp`. In md 876 `comp >= 30` sets `DamageType = comp` which reads HDAT 40–59 — **undefined/out of range**.\n" +
+        "- **1..49 with `WALL` 2 or 3 (or `bForceWall`)**: if `Y > ground` → SE 11, snap to the ground, `DamageOldIndex = 0`, `DamageOldType = comp` (md 876) or 16 (md 877), `DamageType = 12` (the bounce reaction). Else, if at a world-edge wall (below), set `DamageWall = true` and switch to type `comp`.\n" +
+        "- **≥ 50 (including 255)**: if `Y > ground`: SE 12, ANO 13, `DamageEnd`, md 893 (hard-landing stun, jogo:21173-21184).\n" +
+        "- The wall test (both need `(PlayerState[0]|PlayerState[1]) & 1 == 0`, i.e. no flag-1024 blackout): left `X <= iBackXPos + halfWidth && (iBaseXPos <= halfWidth || bForceWall)`; right `X >= iBackXPos + 31391744 - halfWidth && (iBaseXPos + halfWidth >= 62849024 || bForceWall)`. Md 876 also requires `DamageYSpeed <= 0`; md 877 treats `WALL == 3` as a permanent wall and handles `comp >= 30`.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**`WALL` column [CODE].** 0/1: the wall does not restart the reaction; 1 also makes the camera pan to follow the wall-hit player (md 19, jogo:15380-15426). 2/3: touching the wall (or landing) restarts the reaction at `COMP`; 3 additionally keeps `iBaseXPos += iBackXOffset` (no recentre). `bForceWall` is reset every tick in md 935 and set by cutscene effect kind 6 (jogo:25231-25232).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**md 876 vs 877 [CODE].** Same pipeline (jogo:20983 vs 21259). Differences: table source (gamedata HDAT 10+type vs the attacker's character HDAT 14+type); 877 first forces ANO 0 if the new ANO equals the current one (restart) and calls `ChrSePlay`; type 2 → 29 on KO only in 876; the wall branch differs as above; landing sets `PlayerAir = false` in 876 but not in 877's COMP 11/generic landing; bounce `DamageOldType` is `comp` in 876 and 16 in 877; 877 ending airborne explicitly moves to md 876 types 13/2. Character reactions (877) can chain to gamedata types 1–29 or character types 30–49; gamedata reactions (876) only to gamedata types 1–29.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**DamageChange vs DamageEnd [CODE].** `DamageChange` (jogo:3466) starts a reaction; `DamageEnd` (jogo:4043) ends it and zeroes `PlayerAttack`, `SpecialKind/Type`, `DamageType/Index`, sets `ComboCount[1-p] = 0`, `HitActNo = -1`, `BulletAction[p][0] = 0`, `ThrowDamage = DamageWall = false`, `DamageHitSpecialType = 20`. It does **not** touch `DamageTime`, the speeds, `DamageOld*` or `DamageMove`. State variables: progress = `DamageType/Index/Time`; chain origin = `DamageOldType/OldIndex`; persistent speeds = `DamageXSpeed/YSpeed/XAccel/YAccel` (not cleared by `DamageEnd`); landing = `DamageWall`, `bForceWall`, `DefensiveFlag`; source = `DamageHitActNo`, `DamageHitSpecialType`.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Return to normal [CODE].** Table ends with `DamageYSpeed == 0` and life > 0 → `DamageEnd` → md 864 → md 872. Airborne at the end → type 13; md 864 with `Y < ground && !PlayerAir` plays ANO 89 and md 886 (jogo:20748-20755). Hard landing md 887/893 (jogo:22150-22281). Lying: md 889 waits for the lying animation, md 890 does `DamageEnd` and plays ANO 25, md 894 returns to md 864 (jogo:22166-22199, 22283-22288). A new hit is possible any time a hurtbox overlaps; `ComboCount` resets only on the defender's `DamageEnd`.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**KO table lookups and trades.** KO forces type 2 whatever OPT1 was (see 15.4). A trade forces OPT1 = 0 (see 15.4). Clash of attack boxes (below) puts the loser in a reaction taken from the counter-user's `charHDAT3[0][13]` (types ≥ 30 → md 877, else md 876): this is the reaction used by `ATK_FLAGS` bit 2 (NO_TRADE), and it is that **number** the app prints in the GOLPE SET explanation.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 15.6 Physics and movement (questions 46–52)\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Coordinates [CODE].** Fixed point 16.16 for `PlayerXPos`, `PlayerYPos`, `obj.x/y` and the animation `iXSpeed/iYSpeed/iXAccel/iYAccel` (32-bit little-endian in the pattern, jogo:31913-31937). Ground is `PlayerYPos = 15728640` (240 px); **Y grows downward**; `Y > ground` is below the floor. Visible screen width 31391744 (479 px), world width 62849024 (959 px), `iBaseXPos` starts at 31457280 (jogo:5554), scroll zones at 4587520 and 26869760. `obj.x = PlayerXPos - iBackXPos (- iBackXOffset)`. Half width `hw = charHDAT3[0][3]/2` px. There is **no global gravity and no speed clamp** in the engine; gravity is a per-pattern `iYAccel` in the animation script or the accel columns of a reaction row.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Order of update inside one tick [CODE].**\n" +
+        "- *Animation script* (`_ActReqMain`, jogo:31804-31842): `x += iXSpeed` (or `-=` when `wObjFlag & 16`, facing left), `y += iYSpeed` (or `-=` when `wObjFlag & 32`), then `iXSpeed += iXAccel`, `iYSpeed += iYAccel`, then `--time`. A pattern of duration T gets T moves with speeds s0, s0+a, s0+2a…; the load tick moves nothing. At pattern load speed is zeroed unless `wActFlag & 64` (keep speed) and accel is **always** zeroed (jogo:31901-31907).\n" +
+        "- *Reaction (md 876/877)*: on the entry tick speeds are loaded and the position moves with them; on later ticks (hitstop = 0) it **accelerates first** (`speed += accel`) **then moves** — the opposite of animation scripts. **X friction**: after accelerating X, if the sign flipped, or the old value was ≤ 0 and the new is > 0, or the new is 0 → `DamageXSpeed = 0` and `DamageXAccel = 0` (jogo:21075-21078), so X cannot accelerate from rest. Y has no clamp. `+speed` moves in the facing direction (flag 16 → `X -= speed<<9`, jogo:21082-21088); defenders face the attacker, so knock-back uses negative speeds unless the reaction ANO is negative (flipped).\n" +
+        "- *Per-tick sequence for a defender*: reaction speed update → reaction move → `PlayerTail` (jogo:29714-29899): applies `DamageMove`, `_SetXY`, `_ActReq` (animation script movement) and writes `PlayerXPos` back. So the **reaction speed and the animation-script speed both apply in the same tick**; then `CheckOptFlag` runs. `DamageMove` (guard push) moves `X ± DamageMove<<15` then `DamageMove -= 2` (floor 0).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Ground, air, landing [CODE].** Airborne = `PlayerYPos != 15728640` and `PlayerAir`. Attack landing: md 883 checks `Y > ground && iYSpeed > 0` → SE 12, `Y = ground`, then the HDAT 4 landing ANO (`POUSO_AO_ERRAR` / `POUSO_AO_ACERTAR`) or ANO 13 and md 893 (jogo:21958-21995). Free air movement in md 886 snaps to the ground and enters md 887 (jogo:22141-22147). Falling after an airborne animation ends: ANO 89 (fixed).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Screen and walls [CODE].** Camera task md 19: clamp `X ∈ [iBackXPos+hw, iBackXPos+31391744-hw]` when `iBackXOffset == 0`, no scroll target, not md 911..915 and not `ScreenEdgeOff` (jogo:15537-15562; `ScreenEdgeOff` is set by cutscene kinds 7/8/9). World-edge test uses `iBaseXPos == 0` or `62849024`. Grounded players are kept apart by `(w0+w1)/2` (`ATK_FLAGS` bit 16 \"GHOST\" disables that separation near the floor). Corner push-back: a player pushed into the edge while the opponent is attacking pushes the opponent back by 80 % of the penetration (jogo:15159-15171).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Bounce, ricochet, continuous fall [CODE].** There is **no automatic velocity reflection**. A bounce is a new reaction row with its own speeds: gamedata type 12 on a WALL 2/3 landing, the `comp` types, type 13 at the end of a table, type 2 / duration 255 timeouts.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Facing [CODE].** `wObjFlag & 16` = facing left (set for player 1 at start; bit 32 flips Y). It sets the movement sign of animation scripts, the hitbox mirror (`(wActFlag & 48) ^ (wObjFlag & 48)`, jogo:2058-2096) and projectile/effect spawn sides. `DamageChange` turns the defender toward the attacker (unless it is within half-width of the matching screen edge and facing the wall); `StartPlayerAttack` turns the attacker toward the opponent (jogo:31625-31634). A negative reaction ANO flips again.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Sources of movement [CODE].** (1) the attacker's animation script (speed/accel/keep-bit); (2) the defender's reaction rows; (3) projectile scripts (md 971: `_work[2]/[3]` world-absolute; `obj.x = _work[2] - iBackXPos - iBackXOffset`, `_ActReq`, back to `_work`; facing from the owner; optional homing; clamped to `Y <= ground` then a ground-impact animation or death); (4) teleports: hit flags 39/40 (jogo:2314-2337) and cutscene kinds 10..15 (jogo:25244-25268); (5) guard push `DamageMove`; (6) `PlayerTail` separation/clamps.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Minimum parameters to reproduce a move's physics without simulating the scene [CODE].** Attack/projectile: per pattern the duration (`$TIME`), `$MOVE` speed/accel (px per tick as the editor prints them) and the keep-speed bit, the facing, start position and the floor. Reaction: per row `DUR_C/DUR_A`, ground and air `xs, ys, xa, ya`, `COMP`, `WALL`, `ANO`, plus the chain through `COMP`, hitstop, facing, start `X/Y`. Not data-driven: screen/wall geometry (half width from HDAT 3, the constants above) and the guard/KO decisions.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 15.7 Projectiles and sub-projectiles (questions 53–63)\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Creation [CODE].** A projectile appears when the attacker's current pattern contains a hit-box entry of **type 0** and `BulletAction[p][0] != 0 && BulletNum < 8` (`PlayerTail`, jogo:29808-29878). `BulletAction[p][0]` was chosen at `StartPlayerAttack` (jogo:31664-31672) from HDAT 4: byte 4 (`PROJETIL_ANIM_NORMAL`) when `PlayerYPos[att] < PlayerYPos[opp] + 3342336` and `> PlayerYPos[opp] - 2424832`, byte 34 (`PROJETIL_ANIM_ABAIXO`) when the attacker is ≥ 51 px lower, byte 36 (`PROJETIL_ANIM_ACIMA`) when ≥ 37 px higher. `BulletAction[p][1]` = byte 6 (`PROJETIL_ANIM_AO_ACERTAR`). The spawned task md 970 (prio 13312+p) does `_SetAct(p+3, ano)` and `_SetObj(153+4p)` (jogo:24534-24535): **the projectile's animation is an ordinary ANO of the same character DAC** (`ChrGameData[p+3]`). **Count**: 1 per type-0 entry; **3 projectiles** (ANO, ANO+1, ANO+2) when `SpecialKind & 4`. **Position**: attacker `PlayerXPos ± (hit.x << 16)` (mirrored by facing), `Y + (hit.y << 16)`; `SpecialKind & 32` → at the opponent's X/Y; `& 64` → opponent's X on the ground. After spawning, the hit entry's type is set to −1 (spawns once per pattern). Limits: `BulletNum < 8` per player, and at most 16 registered hit-capable objects per owner (`iTCBReqNum < 16`).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Loop md 971 [CODE]** (jogo:24545-24698). World-absolute position in `_work[2]/[3]`; each tick `obj.x = _work[2] - iBackXPos - iBackXOffset`, `_ActReq` (the ANO script moves it with `$MOVE` speed/accel — **the projectile's speed, direction and trajectory are the ANO's `$XSPEED/$YSPEED/$XACCEL/$YACCEL`**, mirrored by the owner's facing stored in `_work[6]`), then back to `_work`. Death when its ANO ends (`wActFlag & 2`, jogo:24549) or on contact rules below. `Y` is clamped to the ground: touching it switches to the floor ANO (`_work[13]` = byte 40 `PROJETIL_COLISAO_CHAO`) or dies (jogo:24575-24598). It runs `CheckOptFlag` unless frozen, so a projectile ANO can carry hit-flag actions (shake, dust, sub-projectile spawn…), but those land on the **owner's** `PlayerState`.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Hit handling [CODE].** Collision is a normal attack-box vs hurtbox test (`tcbReqHit[]`, jogo:23383-23428); skipped if either player's `wObjFlag & 8` or a counter/clash already happened this tick. On a hit: `DamageChange` with the **owner's** `AttackMul`/flags and the projectile's current `OptData[0]` (damage) and `OptData[1]` (reaction); target hit-stop = full, projectile hit-stop = half, owner not frozen; `HitTarget[tgt] = 1`; `DamageHitSpecialType[tgt] = _work[11]`. If the projectile's SpecialType equals the owner's current one: `CancelTime = 20` and `wFlag |= 4096` on the owner (jogo:24560-24566), which makes the **attacker** switch to the alternate hit ANO (`ANIM_AO_ACERTAR`, byte 32 — \"SEQ_PROJETIL\") and then arm SEQ/END. After a hit the projectile continues if `SpecialKind & 1` (the editor's \"does not explode on the enemy\"/GROUND_ONLY, jogo:24569), otherwise it switches to the hit ANO (`_work[12]`, byte 38 `PROJETIL_ANIM_ACERTAR_GLOBAL`, or byte 6) or dies. Because each *pattern* with a hit block hits once, **a projectile ANO with several hit-block patterns hits several times** (multi-hit \"beams\"); a pattern without a hit block cannot hit.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Sub-projectiles [CODE].** A type-0 entry inside a projectile ANO spawns a sub-projectile with ANO from byte 18 (`SUBPROJETIL_ANIM_ID`), on-hit ANO byte 20, floor ANO byte 42 (jogo:24658-24695).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Homing and repeats [CODE].** Homing runs only when the bullet is not frozen **and HDAT4 byte 26 (`HOMING`) equals 0** (the field looks inverted: 0 = homing on); speed is byte 28; it uses an atan table and sin table (jogo:24610-24628) — it recomputes the heading every tick **[INFERRED]**. Repeats (md 883, jogo:21997-22028): while `SpecialBulletNumber < HDAT4[30]` (`MAX_REPETICOES`), the frame has `wOptFlag & 512` and the player presses the attack buttons (`JoyTrig & 16640`), ANO 40/41 are swapped and the counter increments; the repeat uses the 512 window, which the grab also uses (a move cannot do both).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Interpretation of the user's GOLPE_9 (Kamehameha) question (Q63/Q90/Q91) [INFERRED from the generic rules].** The role of an ANO is decided **only by which `$GOLPE_n` field points to it**, never by its number. Read `$GOLPE_9`: `ANIM_INICIAL` (the attacker's cast ANO, here 51); `PROJETIL_ANIM_NORMAL/ABAIXO/ACIMA` (the projectile ANO — probably 49 — chosen by height); `PROJETIL_ANIM_AO_ACERTAR` / `ACERTAR_GLOBAL` / `COLISAO_CHAO` (ANOs the projectile switches to on hit/floor — possibly 50); `ANIM_AO_ACERTAR` (the attacker's reaction ANO after the beam connects). Inside the projectile ANO, each frame/pattern with a type-2 box and `$OPT` damage hits **once** per pattern: \"damage 5 and 4, reaction 116, then a frame without hitbox\" means the beam hits in the patterns that carry a hitbox, dealing the formula in 15.4 each time (5 and 4 are `d0` values, 116 = OPT1 group 2 / game reaction 16), with combo scaling reducing later hits, and the pattern without a hitbox cannot hit. The visual (sprites, `$IMG`, `$MID`, `$MOVE` speed) and the collision (type-2 boxes, `$OPT`) are separate data in the same frames.\n" +
+        "**To change only…** *damage*: `$OPT` `d0` of the hitbox frames. *reaction*: `$OPT` `d1` (OPT1). *projectile speed*: `$XSPEED` (and accel) in the projectile ANO's `$MOVE`. *number of hits*: the number of patterns that carry a type-2 box (add/remove hit blocks), and `MAX_REPETICOES` for repeated throws. *impact animation*: `PROJETIL_ANIM_AO_ACERTAR` / `ACERTAR_GLOBAL` (what the projectile becomes) or the attacker's `ANIM_AO_ACERTAR`.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 15.8 ANO, MPT, sprites and links (questions 64–71)\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Structure [CODE].** An ANO (`$ANO_n`) in the DAC = `flags` byte (4 = priority byte present, 2 = link block present), `mpt` byte (pattern/frame count, ≤ 255), optional priority, optional links (6 bytes each: x, y, flags|ANO & 4095; ≤ 13, one level), then an offset table of patterns (`jogo:32354-32366`). A pattern (`$MPT_i`) starts with a **flag byte** that says which fields follow, in this order: `0x20` **TIME** (1 byte; **absent ⇒ `time = 0` and the frame never advances**), the **image** short (always present; `-1` = no sprite), `0x01` **MID** (ox, oy shorts), `0x02` **WACTFLAG** word, `0x08` **SE** byte, `0x04` **MOVE** block (mask bits 1/2/4/8 select `xSpeed/ySpeed/xAccel/yAccel`, 32-bit 16.16 each), `0x10` **HITS** block, `0x40` **OPT** block (`wOptFlag` word + 4 bytes `OptData`), `0x80` **RAZ** block (rotation, alpha, x/y zoom + their per-tick adds). `_ActReqMain` (jogo:31772-32047) runs once per tick per object (root and its 13 links).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Processing of a frame [CODE].** On the tick a pattern is loaded: `time`, `img`, `ox/oy`, `wActFlag &= 0xA000` (only the two sync bits survive) then OR the frame's word; SE (`< 80` → `PushSE(se−1)`: common game sound; `≥ 80` → `var2.se` played by `ChrSePlay` from the character's wav list); **speed zeroed unless `wActFlag & 64`; accel always zeroed**; then the MOVE block loads speeds/accels; hit block rebuilds `hit[]`; OPT block loads `wOptFlag/OptData` (absent ⇒ all 0); RAZ sets rotation/alpha/zoom. On later ticks while `time > 0` (and not frozen by `wActFlag & 4`): tween (`OptData[2] != 0`), move (`x += iXSpeed` mirrored by `wObjFlag & 16`; `y` by bit 32), add accel, `--time`; at 0 the next pattern loads (`pat++`), or `pat = 0` if `wActFlag & 1` (**WACTFLAG bit 1 = loop back to the first frame when this frame ends**), and when `pat >= mpt` the ANO ends (`wActFlag |= 2`).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "",
+        "**WACTFLAG bits [CODE].** `1` loop to frame 0 at the end of this frame · `2` ANO finished (set by the engine) · `4` frozen (engine hit-stop; also checked on the parent) · `16` flip X · `32` flip Y (these two are XORed with `wObjFlag & 48` for drawing and boxes) · `64` keep speed · `0x2000` (8192) follow the parent's position (links) · `0x8000` (32768) follow the parent's frame. Bits `512/1024/2048` are set by the engine in a few places **[UNKNOWN meaning]**. `$TIME: 0`/absent freezes a frame forever (a frozen last frame is a classic way to hold a pose).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Links [CODE].** A link is another ANO spawned with the parent (`lnk[13]`, one level). It follows the parent when its `wActFlag` has `0x2000` (position) / `0x8000` (frame); with the frame sync, if the parent's `pat` changed the link jumps to the same `pat` and restarts its `time`. Hit boxes/flags inside links are **not processed** (collision and `CheckOptFlag` are root-only), and a link's own links are not created.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Image, origin, draw order [CODE].** `img` indexes the character's CNV (9 bytes per entry: sheet, x, y, w, h; `DrawImage` jogo:620). `img = -1` (or an ANO without data) draws nothing but the frame still counts time, moves and carries boxes/OPT/SE. The sprite is drawn centred around the object's position offset by `MID` (ox, oy), zoomed/rotated by RAZ. Draw order is a global sort by priority (`prio − iActPrio`, then task priority); a character's ANO may carry `$PRIO`. **Visual vs. collision are independent**: a frame may have a sprite and no boxes, boxes and no sprite, or neither.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Animation changes during an attack [CODE].** On hit: SEQ/END/`ANIM_AO_ACERTAR` (15.1); landing: `POUSO_AO_ERRAR/ACERTAR` or ANO 13; end of airborne animation: ANO 89; wall/KO/reaction end: ANO 24/25/13/89 by state (15.5). Hit flag **20** (cutscene) spawns task md 996 which plays an ANO from `effect.pac` or the character's pac in parallel and may freeze the opponent, move the camera and force walls (rows of HDAT 13; 15.9).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 15.9 Effects, sounds, camera (questions 72–76)\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Hit effect and sound [CODE].** After `DamageChange` the game spawns the effect given by `HitEffectActNo[group]` = `{0, 0, 1, 0, -1}` (effect-pack ANO 0 or 1; group 4 none) at `iHitXPos/iHitYPos` through md 965/966 on `ChrGameData[5]` (the `effect` pack), and plays `HitSound[group]` = `{3,4,6,3,7}` (SE 8 when the effect is neither ANO 0 nor 1). Guard uses `GuardEffectActNo` = `{2,2,2,2,-1}` and SE 8. Clash spark = effect ANO 3 + SE 9. These come from the OPT1 **group**, i.e. from the attacker's `$OPT` `d1`, not from HDAT 4.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Effects created by hit flags [CODE].** Flags 10–17: effect-pack ANO `50 + flag − 10` (dust/smoke). Flags 41–70: `charf` pack ANO `flag − 41 + 3` (bubbles; never mirrored). Flags 71–125: the **character's own DAC**, ANO `201 + flag − 71` (auras/effects; inherit the owner's flip unless the effect's frame has a type-0 box). They live while the flag is present in the owner's current frame (tracked in `AuraAction[player][63]`, md 976/978), at offset `(hit.x, hit.y)` mirrored by facing. `wOptFlag` bits 4096·t (t = 1..15): dust task md 961 at the feet (t 1–5 → bobj ANO 10–14, 6–7 → effect ANO 78–79, ≥ 8 → effect ANO 70+(t−8); +80 when facing left); bit 2048: wall-impact effect (effect ANO 12, SE 6, `CancelTime[opp] = 0`, only after `DamageWall`); bit 1024: `PlayerState |= 1` (hides the background, blocks wall detection).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Camera, shake, zoom [CODE].** Hit flags 3/4/5 set `iBackShakeType` and `iBackShake = 12` (light/medium/strong shake). Flags 30/31 set action-zoom variables (`iZoomBase`, `iZoomXCenter`, focus time). Hit-focus (md 994/995) zooms on a hit. md 19 is the camera/scroll task (13745): follows the players, clamps them to the screen (15.6), and reacts to `DamageWall` for WALL 1/3. `bActionStop`/`iTaskSleep` pause all gameplay tasks (used by ultimates/cutscenes).\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Sound and voice [CODE].** Frame `$SE < 80`: common game sound `SE−1` via `PushSE`; `≥ 80`: character wav `SE` via `ChrSePlay` (sorted `*.wav`, id 80 = first). Reaction `VOZ > 0`: `Voice(1, player, id)` when the row is entered. Wall impact SE 6, landing SE 12, bounce SE 11.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**Cutscenes (md 996) [CODE].** Created by hit flag 20 (`CheckOptFlag`, jogo:2284; prio 13729): row `id` of the **attacker's HDAT 13** (stride `2*XSize[13]`): [0] actor type (0 = effect pack ANO via `ChrGameData[5]`, 1 = the character's own pac, other = bobj pack), [2] pattern window (kills the task when the attacker passes `pat >= _work[3] + value`), [4] priority mode, [6]/[8] ANO facing right/left, [10] mode (1 = full-screen), [12] freeze the opponent (md 925 until the scene ends: projectiles, auras and grabs also pause), [14] special action 1–15 (3/4/7/9 `ScrollCheckOff`, 5 `iScrollTarget`, 6 `bForceWall`, 7/8/9 `ScreenEdgeOff`, 10–15 teleports to a screen edge). It sets `PlayerState |= 33554432` while it exists.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**What belongs where [CODE].** HDAT 4: which ANOs a move uses (start, projectile, SEQ/END, landing, grab, sub-projectile) and the `ATK_FLAGS`. The ANO frames: sprites, timing, movement, boxes, `$OPT` (damage, reaction code, interpolation), `wOptFlag` bits (windows, dust, wall impact, background), hit-flag actions (shake, zoom, cutscene, teleport, aura/effect spawn, heal, self-damage…). `effect`/`gamedata`: the hit/guard/clash effect ANOs, the reaction tables, the combo-scaling table, the dust/smoke ANOs. **Logic vs. visual**: flags 20 (freeze/camera/walls), 26–28, 32, 34, 37–40, `wOptFlag` 512/1024/2048, ATK_FLAGS and OPT1 groups change gameplay; sprites, `MID`, RAZ, shake (3–5), dust and aura effects (10–17, 41–125) are visual/audio only; zoom (30/31) affects only the camera.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "### 15.10 Flags and special behaviours (questions 77–81 and 10–12)\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "There are **four different flag spaces**; never mix them.\n" +
+        "\n" +
+        "**(a) `ATK_FLAGS` = HDAT 4 byte 0 = `SpecialKind[p]` [CODE].** `1` projectile survives hitting the opponent (keeps flying; jogo:24569) · `2` the move's hitbox **destroys/beats the opponent's attack boxes** and forces the opponent into the reaction stored in the *attacker's* `HDAT3[0][13]` (clash handling, jogo:23286, 23339, 23486-23516) · `4` throw 3 projectiles (jogo:29812) · `8` simple grab · `128` conditional grab (only while the opponent is in this move's hurt reaction; grabs work in moves 0–12) (jogo:21929) · `16` stop the camera push — characters pass through each other (jogo:15176) · `32` projectile spawns at the opponent's X/Y · `64` at the opponent's X on the ground (jogo:29822-29827). Bits 256+ unused **[UNKNOWN]**. Flags 8/128 and `MAX_REPETICOES` share the frame window 512.\n" +
