+        "**(c) `wOptFlag` bits (the `$OPT` `$FLAG` word) [CODE].** `256` survives the mask, **no reader found** [UNKNOWN] · `512` chain/cancel/repeat/grab window (read by md 882/883: advancing to `ano+1` on grab, repeat-fire, cancel timing) · `1024` `PlayerState |= 1` (hide background, suppress wall detection; blackout/super marker) · `2048` wall-impact effect (needs `DamageWall`) · `4096·t` (t 1..15) dust/smoke selector. After each pass `wOptFlag &= 1792` so 2048 and the dust bits fire once, 256/512/1024 persist for the pattern.\n" +
